# Inventory Close Gaurd — environment example
#
# NAMES ONLY. Never commit a real value to this file.
#
# This prototype requires NO environment variables. That is a property of the
# design rather than an omission from this file:
#
#   * The FY2026 dataset is generated in-process from the recorded seed
#     ICG-FY2026-DEMO-002. There is no database, and nothing to connect to.
#   * NetSuite is represented by committed synthetic fixtures behind a
#     read-only adapter. There is no NetSuite account, endpoint or credential.
#   * No AI provider is bound. Ask Gaurd's answers are produced by a
#     deterministic engine over the same services the screens use, so there is
#     no model key to supply and the demo works with AI unavailable.
#
# `pnpm install && pnpm build && pnpm --filter @icg/web start` is the whole
# configuration story. A grep for `process.env` across apps/ and packages/
# returns nothing, and `test/synthetic-and-secrets.test.ts` fails the build if
# a credential-shaped literal is ever added.
#
# Names a HOST may set (both are supplied by the platform — Vercel sets them
# for you, and neither is read by application code):
#
# NODE_ENV=
# PORT=
